    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          2
        ],
        "content": "## Pick the cheapest carrier for shipped orders with EasyPost and Claude\n\nE-commerce operations teams that choose carriers by habit and answer 'where is my order' by hand.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: The WMS or e-commerce platform (Shopify, NetSuite, ShipStation) posts when a shipment is packed.\n1. Receive the shipment\n2. Rate across carriers\n3. Select the service\n4. Book and label\n5. Track in flight\n6. Detect and explain delays\n7. Notify and escalate\n8. Audit carrier invoices\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus EasyPost / Shippo / carrier APIs, Gmail / Zendesk, Google Sheets / Postgres.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nPut your carrier accounts and service rules in the Config node; connect the order webhook to Shopify, NetSuite or ShipStation.\nGuardrail to keep: Customer messages for orders above a value threshold are approved by a person before sending.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/logistics-optimization/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
